   "text": "I read the image region by region, then worked out each stereocentre from its wedge.\n\n**Fragments read from the drawing**\n- **Left end:** a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group on the nitrogen of an isoindolin-1-one. The isoindolinone carries an alkyne on the ring carbon next to the CH2-bearing carbon.\n- **Linker:** the alkyne is followed by five CH2 groups and then a C=O. That C=O is the acyl group on the ring nitrogen of the central bicycle.\n- **Central bicycle:** an eight-membered ring made of N(acyl), CH2, CH(NH-acyl), C(=O), N, a ring-fusion CH, CH2 and CH2. It is fused through the N and the fusion CH to a pyrrolidine. The pyrrolidine CH next to N carries the carboxamide.\n- **NH-acyl group:** a benzothiophene-2-carboxamide with a CF2\u2013PO3H2 group at C5.\n- **Right-hand side:** the carboxamide nitrogen bonds to a CH that carries a CH2CH2C(=O)NH2 chain and a thiazol-2-yl group. The thiazole has a 4-chlorophenyl at C4.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The glutarimide CH is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo label.\n- The four wedged centres are the NH-bearing ring CH, the pyrrolidine CH, the ring-fusion CH and the side-chain CH. I assigned each from the wedge direction, with the implicit H pointing away from the viewer.\n\nI checked ring closures and atom counts by hand, but did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(C(=O)N1)N1Cc2c(cccc2C#CCCCCCC(=O)N2C[C@H](NC(=O)c3cc4cc(C(F)(F)P(=O)(O)O)ccc4s3)C(=O)N3[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)c4nc(-c5ccc(Cl)cc5)cs4)CC[C@@H]3CC2)C1=O"
